cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these analysis materials, please cite this software release."
type: software
title: "CamKIT-AI: analysis code, fitted-pipeline specification and aggregate study results"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Castagno
    given-names: Simone
    affiliation: "Department of Surgery, University of Cambridge"
repository-code: "https://github.com/simocasta/camkit-ai-analysis"
url: "https://github.com/simocasta/camkit-ai-analysis"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, fitted-pipeline specification, archived software-environment
  provenance, synthetic input examples and non-disclosive aggregate results
  supporting a secondary transportability and software-reproducibility analysis
  of a machine-learning triage model for acute soft-tissue knee injury using
  patient-completed questionnaires. Participant-level inputs, record-level
  predictions and the fitted model are not included. These public materials
  support inspection and testing of the analysis utilities but do not permit
  independent regeneration of the reported predictions.
keywords:
  - acute knee injury
  - machine learning
  - triage
  - transportability
  - software reproducibility
